BlockingAngle [SimTalk]
Sets the Blocking Angle of the PickAndPlace robot designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The Blocking Angle is the angle in degrees which the PickAndPlace robot cannot cross. It prevents the
robot from taking the shortest way.
The Blocking Angle only affects the animation, the simulation is controlled by the rotation times which
you defined in the Times Table.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.BlockingAngle:real
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type real.
You can specify an angle between 0 and 360 degrees.
The default setting -1 means that no blocking angle applies and that the robot thus takes the shortest way.
Example
MyPickAndPlace.BlockingAngle := 5
See also
Blocking Angle [text box]
Times Table [PickAndPlace]
BlockingAngle [SimTalk]
11-1958 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Capacity [SimTalk] - PickAndPlace
Sets the Capacity of the PickAndPlace robot designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The Capacity is the number of MUs that the PickAndPlace robot can transport at any one time.
The capacity enables the PickAndPlace robot to transport more than one part at the same time. It might,
for example, pick up a number of bottles and place same into the appropriate slots of a bottle crate one at
a time (FIFO).
If you want to unload the parts according to another rule, for example LIFO, you can program this in an
Exit Control.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Capacity:integer
Watchable
The attribute is watchable.
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type integer.
Specify a value greater than 1.
Example
MyPickAndPlace.Capacity := 12
See also
Capacity [text box] - PickAndPlace
Capacity [SimTalk] - PickAndPlace
Plant Simulation Help 11-1959
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

DefaultAngle [SimTalk] - PickAndPlace
Sets the Default Angle of the PickAndPlace robot designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The Default Angle is the rotation angle in degrees to which the side of the end point of the PickAndPlace
robot rotates when you set GoToDefaultPosition to true.
To rotate the PickAndPlace robot to the side on which the start point is located, add 180° to this angle.
Note
The Default Angle is also used as the start position after a Reset, no matter if Go to Default Position is
activated or not.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.DefaultAngle:real
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type real.
Specify a value between 0 ° and 360 °.
Example
MyPickAndPlace.DefaultAngle := 5
