MUConveyingDirection [SimTalk]
Sets the conveying direction of the MU on the PickAndPlace robot designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Note
For the settings Retain, Rotate by 90° to the right, Rotate by 90° to the left, and Rotate by 180° the
PickAndPlace robot executes a relative rotation depending on the direction from which the MU arrives.
For the settings Forwards, Lateral right, Backwards, and Lateral left the rotation is an absolute
rotation independent of the direction from which the MU arrives.
Conveying
direction Description Looks like this
Retain The robot continues conveying
the part in the same direction in
which it arrives.
Rotate 90° to
the right
The robot rotates the part 90°
to the right and places it on the
successor.
Rotate 90° to
the left
The robot rotates the part 90°
to the left and places it on the
successor.
Rotate 180° The robot rotates the part 180°
and places it on the successor.
Forwards The robot rotates the part, so
that it comes to rest on the
successor forward and then
places it on the successor.
MUConveyingDirection [SimTalk]
11-1964 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Conveying
direction Description Looks like this
Lateral right The robot rotates the part,
so that it comes to rest on
the successor laterally to the
right and then places it on the
successor.
Backwards The robot rotates the part, so
that it comes to rest on the
successor backward and then
places it on the successor.
Lateral left The robot rotates the part,
so that it comes to rest on
the successor laterally to the
left and then places it on the
successor.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.MUConveyingDirection:string
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
You can specify "Retain", "Rotate 90° to the right", "Rotate 90° to the left",
"Rotate 180°", "Forwards", "Lateral right", "Backwards", or "Lateral left".
Example
MyPickAndPlace.MUConveyingDirection := "Forwards"
