PullCtrl [SimTalk] - PickAndPlace
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation calls the Pull Control whenever the PickAndPlace robot is ready to pick up a new part or
when it is ready when a new MU is Waiting at its entrance.
If you set TargetSelection to "Load part onto MU at sensor" the PickAndPlace robot only counts
as ready if a Container/Transporter is waiting at the sensor. This also applies if you programmed a Pull
Control. It will only be called when a Container/Transporter is waiting at the sensor.
In the Pull Control you can determine which of the parts, which intends to move onto the object, the
PickAndPlace robot will accept. For this you have to get the forward blocking list of the object with the
method fwBlockList and unblock a MU in the list with the method unblock.
Let us assume that red parts are especially important and thus have priority for being processed. Then you
can always pull red parts first from the predecessors and only then pull parts in other colors.
Note
The Pull Control does not determine if a MU is to be moved to this or to another successor. Instead, it
selects one of the parts which have already been determined to move on to this successor.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.PullCtrl:method
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Example
MyPickAndPlace.PullCtrl := &myPullControl
See also
Pull Control [PickAndPlace]
PullCtrl [SimTalk] - PickAndPlace
Plant Simulation Help 11-1967
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

TargetCtrl [SimTalk] - PickAndPlace
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Plant Simulation runs the Target Control as soon as the PickAndPlace robot designated by <Path> has
completely picked up the part. In this control you determine the successor onto which the PickAndPlace
robot deposits the part.
As opposed to the Exit Control, the part is not ready to exit the object yet. You have to set the target
object in the method setDestination.
Plant Simulation also calls the control when the PickAndPlace robot has deposited the part. In this case
you have to set the object, at which the robot is going to pick up the next part with the method
setDestination.
When the PickAndPlace robot calls the Target Control after depositing the part, the active element (@) is
void.
Plant Simulation only calls the Target Control while unloading if you cleared the check box Go to Default
Position.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.TargetCtrl:method
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Examples
if ?.empty 
   return 
   end
if @.LastStation = Source 
TargetCtrl [SimTalk] - PickAndPlace
11-1968 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

   ?.setDestination(Drain)
elseif @.LastStation = Source1 
   ?.setDestination(Station, true)
else
   ?.setDestination(Drain1)
end
MyPickAndPlace.TargetCtrl := &myTargetControl
