TargetSelection [SimTalk]
Sets how the PickAndPlace robot designated by <Path> selects the target for the part that is to be moved:
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.TargetSelection:string
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
You can specify:
• "Exit strategy or target control": Default behavior of previous versions of the PickAndPlace
robot. You either set the target with the selected Exit Strategy or you define the target in the Target
Control.
• "Load part onto MU at sensor": For this setting you have to manually create a front-triggered
sensor with light-barrier mode on the length-oriented target object. In addition you have to enter the
Target Object and the Target sensor ID. Stopping the Container/Transporter, loading and sending the
Container/Transporter on only works automatically if you did not enter a control. If you use a control,
you have to program stopping and sending the Container/Transporter on in this control.
Note
The PickAndPlace robot only picks the part to be loaded up at the sensor when a Container/
Transporter is waiting at the sensor.
This also applies if you programmed a PullCtrl. It will only be called when a Container/Transporter is
waiting at the sensor.
• "Place part at sensor": For this setting you have to manually create a rear-triggered sensor with
light barrier mode on the length-oriented target object. In addition you have to enter the Target Object
and the Target Sensor ID.
Example
MyPickAndPlace.TargetSelection := "Load part onto MU at sensor"
See also
Target Object
TargetSelection [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-1971
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

