UseKinematicsForTimes [SimTalk]
Sets if the PickAndPlace robot designated by <Path> uses 3D kinematics to determine its timing (true)
instead of the times defined in the Angles Table and in the Times Table or not (false).
Remarks
The PickAndPlace robot can only use the 3D kinematics if Plant Simulation finds supported robot
kinematics as described under Configuring the Robot.
Note
3D kinematics can either be kinematics that are part of a robot graphic, which you import or 3D
kinematics which are defined in Plant Simulation.
Plant Simulation supports all kinematics that it also supports for the other objects for
using the functions _3D.Poses.moveToCoordinate [SimTalk], _3D.Poses.moveToMU [SimTalk], and
_3D.Poses.moveToMUAnimationPosition [SimTalk], except for linear robots.
Define the Joint Settings of an Animatable Object on the tab Joint of the animatable objects of the
PickAndPlace robot.
Type
Attribute
UseKinematicsForTimes [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-1977
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Syntax
<Path>.UseKinematicsForTimes:boolean
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
Example
MyPickAndPlace.UseKinematicsForTimes := true
