WaitForFreeTarget [SimTalk] -PickAndPlace
Sets if the PickAndPlace robot designated by <Path> only rotates to a part that wants to exit the
predecessor, to pick it up if the destination object is ready to accept it (true) or not (false).
Remarks
Specify false to make the PickAndPlace robot rotate to the part immediately.
Plant Simulation only evaluates WaitForFreeTarget for the setting Target Selection > Exit strategy or
target control.
Plant Simulation enters the part that cannot be transported into the Exit Blocking List of the target object.
Note
If you set the attribute to true, Plant Simulation already evaluates the entered Exit Strategy or the
Target Control for the part before the PickAndPlace robot rotates to the part to pick it up.
Plant Simulation enters the thus determined target into the attribute TargetObject.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.WaitForFreeTarget:boolean
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type boolean.
WaitForFreeTarget [SimTalk] -PickAndPlace
Plant Simulation Help 11-1979
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Example
MyPickAndPlace.WaitForFreeTarget := true
